'''Hype Fazon''' was a [[Rodian]] [[Gender|male]] [[pilot]] from [[Rodia]] who served with [[Ace Squadron]], a team of highly skilled [[starfighter]] pilots tasked with the defense of the ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Fuel|refueling]] station during the [[New Republic Era|era]] of the [[New Republic]]. Operating under the [[callsign]] "[[Ace leader|Ace One]]," Fazon piloted the [[starship]] ''[[Green Ace]]''&mdash;an extravagant ship designed for speed and maximum maneuverability.

In addition, the Aces participated in the station's racing competitions, with Fazon developing his reputation as the [[squadron]]'s top [[racer]]. His exceptional piloting skills attracted the attention of many high-end sponsors whose logos Fazon added to his ship's hull in return for their patronage. As his fame increased, Fazon also became known for his pomposity, bravado, and enormous ego.

==Biography==
===Ace Squadron===
<!-- If this is from an episode. Please locate the episode and source it properly, not ref the youtube video. Remove this comment once done.-->
{{Quote|Ace One to squadron, Light 'em up!|Hype Fazon|<ref name="BTS">{{SWYouTube|MDtY2vVlfaQ|The Aces &#124; Star Wars Resistance|sw_url=video/disneyxd-meet-the-aces-star-wars-resistance}}</ref>}}
[[File:HypeWins-TheRecruitPart2.png|thumb|left|250px|Fazon celebrating another race victory.]]
Hype Fazon was born sometime during the [[Imperial Era|Era]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] on the planet [[Rodia]]. He trained to race in the [[Voxx Cluster]], a racetrack owned by the swindling [[Hutt]], [[Vranki]] the Blue, owner of a [[Vranki's Hotel and Casino|hotel and casino]]. In the [[Standard year|years]] following the [[Galactic Civil War]], Hype left Vranki and resided on the [[ocean]] [[planet]] [[Castilon]] in the [[Western Reaches]] of the [[Mid Rim Territories]] of [[the galaxy]]. During the [[New Republic Era|Era]] of the [[New Republic]],<ref name="The Recruit" /> Fazon became known as one of the most talented [[pilot]]s on the ''[[Colossus]]'',<ref name="Fazon DB" /> a large [[Fuel|refueling]] [[Supertanker fuel depot|station]] located on Castilon.<ref name="The Recruit" /> In his early days on the ''Colossus'', he was friends with fellow racer [[Tamara Ryvora]]. However, they fell out of contact after Fazon earned a place in [[Ace Squadron]], a group of the best pilots on the platform.<ref name="The High Tower">{{Resistance|The High Tower}}</ref> As Squadron Leader, he had the callsign "[[Ace leader|Ace One]]."<ref name="Aces" /> In addition, his personal [[starfighter]] was designated ''[[Green Ace]]'' due to its appearance and affiliation.<ref name="Green Ace DB">{{Databank|green-ace|Green Ace}}</ref> Together, Ace Squadron flew defense for the ''Colossus'',<ref name="Aces">{{SW|url=news/meet-the-aces-in-a-new-star-wars-resistance-featurette|text=Meet the Aces in a New ''Star Wars Resistance'' Featurette}}</ref> and therefore, protected the platform from various threats to its security.<ref name="Fazon DB" />

Like his teammates, Fazon competed in the ''Colossus''{{'}} racing tournaments,<ref name="The Recruit" /> which became the source of his fame. In [[time]] he became known as Ace Squadron's top [[racer]],<ref name="Fazon DB" /> and by [[34 ABY]] had not lost a race in two years.<ref name="The High Tower" /> As his popularity increased, Fazon acquired the patronage of numerous high-end sponsors&mdash;including [[Z'Vk'Thkrkza|Aunt Z's]] [[Aunt Z's Tavern|Tavern]] and the [[Office of Acquisitions]]<ref name="The Recruit" />&mdash;a fact which Fazon advertised by covering his [[starship]] in their logos.<ref name="Green Ace DB" /> As an Ace, he also participated in supply missions escorting in freighters. However, he refused to participate in any missions involving the [[First Order]] since it was the last [[Imperial Remnants|remnant]] of the Empire that ruled the galaxy when he was a kid so he knew how persistent and dangerous they were.<ref name="The High Tower" />

===Defending the ''Colossus''===
During an [[Attack on the Colossus|attack]] by [[Captain]] [[Kragan Gorr]] and his [[Warbird gang|gang]], Fazon joined fellow Aces [[Freya Fenris]], [[Torra Doza]], the daughter of his old friend [[Commander]] [[Venisa Doza]] who left to join the [[Resistance]] formed by [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel]] hero [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] to protect the New Republic and the galaxy from the First Order, and [[Bo Keevil]] in fighting the [[pirate]]s off. Though Ace Squadron was overwhelmed by the pirates, Resistance [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] jammed the pirates' communications; forcing them to retreat.<ref name="The Triple Dark">{{Resistance|The Triple Dark}}</ref>

===Xiono's first visit===
Some time afterwards, as the ''Colossus'' was experiencing a power outage due to a fuel shortage, Fenris, Keevil, and [[Griff Halloran]] went on a supply mission to escort in a fuel freighter belonging to the First Order. Fazon, as he usually did during missions involving them, instead went down to [[Aunt Z's Tavern]], where he encountered Xiono, the newest colleague of Ryvora who flew in a sky race with Torra, heard her father and Venisa’s husband Captain [[Imanuel Doza]], who owned the ''Colossus'', might be working for the First Order from Aunt Z and was trying to figure out a way into [[Doza Tower]], location of the [[Aces' Lounge]]. Fazon spotted Ryvora sitting at Team ''Fireball''{{'s}} booth, but didn't get a chance to approach her.<ref name="The High Tower" />

[[File:KazSnooping-TheHighTower.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Hype and Tam argue]]
Later, Fazon came across Ryvora and Xiono talking about him in the hallway, as Ryvora was listing off reasons she disliked Fazon. Wanting to repair their friendship, Fazon invited the two of them up to the Aces Lounge, an invitation Xiono was happy to accept. At the lounge, Fazon complimented Xiono on his performance in his [[Race between Kazuda Xiono and Torra Doza|sky race]] with Torra. He shortly got into an argument with Ryvora about the ''[[Fireball]]'', the old racing ship she was repairing that Xiono flew for his sky race with Torra, as he thought she would never become a star racer like him and the members of Ace Squadron with a ship that old. This prompted Ryvora to leave alone, as Xiono had slipped off to do some spying.<ref name="The High Tower" />

===The Platform Classic===
A picture of Hype Fazon appeared during the [[Platform Classic]]. Besides Fazon's fellow Ace pilots, galactic racing champion [[Marcus Speedstar]] and his estranged older brother and Xiono’s employer [[Jarek Yeager]] also participated in the race. Speedstar won the race, enabling him to pay his friend [[Oplock]]'s ransom.<ref name="The Platform Classic">{{Resistance|The Platform Classic}}</ref>

===Xiono's second visit===
Hype and his fellow Aces were in the Aces' Lounge when Xiono visited Doza Tower again as a guest of Torra during a [[Second mission to Doza Tower|mission]] to spy on a meeting between her father and [[Stormtrooper Commander]] [[Pyre]]. During the visit, Hype recounted how he won the [[Sublight Star Five Million]] to Keevil. Hype then requested a round of [[Blue milk|bantha milk]] from [[Jace Rucklin]], a racer who fell on hard times. When Rucklin argued with Xiono who he blamed for wrecking his life because he did not know how dangerous [[coaxium]] was when he powered his racer with it, Hype called for Rucklin again.<ref name="Secrets and Holograms">{{Resistance|Secrets and Holograms}}</ref>

===Casual adventures===
Believing that his [[astromech droid]] [[R4-G77]] needed a new motivator, Hype visited the spare-part merchants [[Flix]] and [[Orka]]'s [[Office of Acquisitions]]. R4-G77 proved uncooperative and struggled with Flix and Orka, who managed to subdue him after some difficulty.<ref name="Unmotivated">{{Resistance|Unmotivated}}</ref>

Later, Torra attempted to topple Hype from his position as number one-ranked Ace. Prior to the race, Torra and Hype exchanged snipes at each other. During the early part of the race, Torra took the lead in her racer ''[[Blue Ace]]''. However, Torra used up most of her booster fuel, allowing Hype to regain the lead. Hype then thanked himself over the intercom much to Torra's chagrin.<ref name="The Need for Speed">{{Resistance|The Need for Speed}}</ref>

While escorting a [[fuel]] convoy, Hype reminded Ace Squadron they all needed to work as a team. Ace Squadron were then contacted by a stricken freighter, who was unable to control his ship's descent to the ''Colossus''. With the ship unable to change course, Hype ordered his fellow Aces to latch onto the freighter in order to slow its descent. The Aces managed to slow down the freighter as it landed on the ''Colossus'', narrowly avoiding an accident.<ref name="Sixty Seconds to Destruction">{{Resistance|Sixty Seconds to Destruction}}</ref>

===Bibo incident===
During the [[Bibo incident]], Hype led the defense of the ''Colossus'' against [[Bibo's mother]], a [[rokkna]] sea monster. When Kaz came to help in the ''Fireball'', Hype initially told the unauthorized ship to clear but accepted Kaz's help. Though they were unable to drive away the sea monster, Kaz's friend [[Neeku Vozo]] managed to appease the creature by returning her child [[Bibo]].<ref name="Bibo">{{Resistance|Bibo (episode)}}</ref>

===Kidnapping of Torra Doza===
Following the [[Torra Doza's abduction|kidnapping]] of Torra, Hype and his pilots were dispatched in pursuit of her kidnappers. Torra got rescued by [[Major]] [[Elrik Vonreg]], who convinced her father to accept the First Order’s protection. Some time later, Hype joined Yeager, Kaz, Torra, her father, Freya, and Bo in becoming members of a [[Citizens' Fleet]] assembled by [[General]] [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] to help the Resistance win their [[Battle of Exegol|final match]] with the First Order on the planet [[Exegol]] in the [[Unknown Regions]].<ref name="Doza Dilemma">{{Resistance|The Doza Dilemma}}</ref>

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|You can't handle the Hype!|Hype Fazon, to Bo Keevil|<ref name="Secrets and Holograms" />}}
Hype Fazon was boastful, vain<ref name="Fazon DB" /> and pompous.<ref name="Green Ace DB" /> He relished the fame that came with his reputation as the top racer of the Aces, a status that fueled his enormous ego and bravado.<ref name="Fazon DB" /> Despite his extravagance and pomposity,<ref name="Green Ace DB" /> however, he cared about the well-being of his fellow Aces.<ref name="Aces" /> He disliked the First Order, and refused to fly any supply missions involving them, considering their slowly-growing influence on the station a problem.<ref name="The High Tower" />

Fazon was a [[Rodian]] [[Gender|male]] with [[Color|blue]] [[eye]]s and green skin. On the front of his flight suit belt his name "Hype" was written in [[Aurebesh]]. Logos from various companies adorned his [[flight suit]]: A patch embellished the shoulder of his [[jacket]], written in [[Outer Rim Basic]],<ref name="The Recruit" /> which bore the logo of [[Old Jho's Pit Stop]] located on Lothal planet.<ref name="Empire Day">{{Rebels|Empire Day (episode)}}</ref> The right breast showed<ref name="The Recruit" /> the symbol of [[Power Sliders]] on [[Abafar]],<ref name="Missing">{{TCW|Missing in Action}}</ref> while the left breast displayed<ref name="The Recruit" /> a motif from [[Admiral Snackbar]] on the same world.<ref name="Missing" /> The right breast of his [[jumpsuit]] showed<ref name="The Recruit" /> the logo of [[79's]] on [[Coruscant]];<ref name="Orders">{{TCW|Orders (episode)}}</ref> while the cube motif of [[Outer Rim Supply Co.]] at [[Stobar Spaceport]]<ref name="Brothers">{{TCW|Brothers (episode)}}</ref> and [[Horizon Base]],<ref name="Droid">{{Rebels|The Forgotten Droid}}</ref> was printed on the abdomen.<ref name="The Recruit" />

Fazon cared about appearances, and had his logo and colors plastered all over his [[Hype Fazon's hangar bay|personal hangar]] so no one mistook who the hangar was used by.<ref name="Bucket's List Disappeared">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-the-disappeared-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 6 Fun Facts from "The Disappeared" - ''Star Wars Resistance''}}</ref>

==Skills and abilities==
{{Quote|Hey everybody, look who it&mdash;oh, you know who it is!|Hype Fazon|<ref name="The High Tower" />}}
Hype Fazon lived up to his reputation as the Aces' most talented racer, notwithstanding his ego, due to his exceptional piloting skills.<ref name="Fazon DB" /> The ''Green Ace'' was designed to be the perfect match for his pompous nature, having been plastered with the names and logos of his [[Galactic Credit Standard|financial]] supporters. Beyond its extravagance, however, Fazon's racer boasted wings that could shift angles for maximum maneuverability while speeding through turns.<ref name="Green Ace DB" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|It's one of the few times I've created a character around the person.|Dave Filoni|<ref name="BTS" />}}
Hype Fazon is a character created for the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' animated series. He is voiced by [[Donald Faison]], whose name and personality inspired the creation of Fazon.<ref name="Aces" /> The majority of the logos he sports were designed and introduced in the series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' and ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''.<ref name="High Tower BL">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-the-high-tower-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 9 Fun Facts from "The High Tower" - ''Star Wars Resistance''}}</ref> Faison landed on the role after a conversation he had with ''Resistance'' showrunner [[Dave Filoni]] during the premiere of [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']], Filoni having seen a [[Wikipedia:Stop-motion|stop-motion]] animated short made by Faison entitled ''Black Stormtrooper'', though Faison at first believed that Filoni didn't have him in mind after he wasn't called for ''Rebels''.<ref name="Resistance Interview">{{WebCite|url=http://www.jedinews.co.uk/film-music-tv/articles/star-wars-is-back-on-tv-with-star-wars-resistance|text=Star Wars Is BACK&hellip;. On TV with Star Wars Resistance!|work=Jedinews.co.uk|archivedate=20190829174401}}</ref>

